1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A quick walkthrough of IIUM KAMS, using a sample workspace.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Use your permitted Google account. New staff accounts require administrator approval.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Check asset totals, pending approvals, and the colour-coded asset status chart.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Open Assets and search by asset tag, name, or serial number.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Select the result to review its location, status, assignment, and history.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Choose Register Asset. Scan its label or enter the tag and serial number manually.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Choose the department and room, set availability, then select Register asset.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Open Scan Asset. Use the camera, upload a label photo, or type the code.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
A recognised asset code opens the matching asset record.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
If the code is not recorded, the system opens registration with the code captured.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Open Borrowing, explain the purpose, and choose the start and return dates.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Administrators review the request and approve it, or reject it with a reason.

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
After approval, check out the asset. Mark it returned when the borrowing ends.

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Staff select an assigned asset, the incident type, discovery time, and location.

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
The report receives a reference number and appears in the user’s incident history.

16
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Enter the resolution, parts replaced, actual cost, and downtime. Select Complete work.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
The request shows its resolution and completed status. Close the request after review.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,000
In Locations, add or edit Kulliyyahs, departments, and units.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Build the location hierarchy: campus, building, floor, and room.

20
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Open Master Data, add a category, or select Edit beside an existing category.

21
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Administrators approve accounts and manage roles, departments, and personal information.

22
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Regular users can update their Position, Phone number, and Staff ID from Profile.

23
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Open Reports and export the asset register as CSV or PDF for review and sharing.

24
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
The mobile view keeps common tasks in the bottom menu for quick access.

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Set up your locations, register your assets, and invite your team.
